+### External Agent-Tool Evaluation
+
+Use `ruby scripts/SaneMaster.rb external_tools` before adopting agent-workflow tools from outside SaneProcess.
+
+The command is read-only and optional by design. It checks tools such as `cass`, `ubs`, `dcg`, `br`/`bv`, and `asb` only when they are already installed, records what their safe probe actually returned, and gives an adopt/watch/skip recommendation. Missing tools stay missing; SaneProcess must not turn third-party `curl | bash` installers into default setup. On non-Mini hosts, `external_tools` is strict Mini-first unless `--local` is passed explicitly.
+
+Default adoption rules:
+- `cass`: strongest candidate, useful as an optional session-history research surface.
+- `ubs`: warning-only trial candidate for changed-file scans; never a hard verify gate until false positives and runtime are measured.
+- `dcg`: mine rule-pack/explain ideas, but keep SaneProcess guards local and fixture-reviewed.
+- `br`/`bv`: useful for large local backlogs, not a replacement for GitHub issues, support inbox, or release blockers.
+- `asb`: useful for explicit agent-config backup workflows, but not part of normal verify/release.
+
+2026-04-25 Mini baseline (source: `ruby scripts/SaneMaster.rb external_tools --json --timeout 30`; TTL: re-check after upstream tool updates):
+- `cass 0.3.7` found real SaneProcess history metadata (`40` conversations, `16161` messages) and can list recent sessions, but lexical search is not usable until the index is repaired.
+- `cass index --full` ingested the local Claude/Codex corpus but failed during lexical rebuild with a shard-count mismatch, so `cass` is not adopted yet.
+- `ubs 5.1.1` starts under Homebrew `bash`, but the Ruby module fetch fails checksum verification, so `ubs` is not safe to wire into `verify`.
+- Current decision: keep the SaneMaster evaluation lane, but do not add any of these tools as default dependencies.
+
