+## Session 113 (2026-04-25)
+
+### Done
+- Evaluated the Dicklesworthstone external agent-workflow tools against SaneProcess and implemented the useful part as an optional evidence lane:
+  - added `ruby scripts/SaneMaster.rb external_tools`
+  - added safe probes for `cass`, `ubs`, `dcg`, `br`/`bv`, and `asb`
+  - added JSON and human output modes
+  - registered `scripts/sanemaster/external_tools_test.rb` in `scripts/test_registry.json`
+  - documented the adoption rules in `DEVELOPMENT.md` and ADR-008 in `ARCHITECTURE.md`
+- Installed and tested the two strongest Homebrew candidates on the Mini:
+  - `cass 0.3.7`
+  - `ubs 5.1.1`
+  - Homebrew `bash` was installed because `ubs` requires Bash 4+ and macOS system Bash is 3.2.
+- Made `external_tools` strict Mini-first by default so it does not silently report the controller machine’s missing tools. `--local` is now an explicit parser-supported escape hatch.
+- Hardened Mini routing by raising the SSH connect timeout to 8 seconds and retrying once before declaring the Mini unreachable.
+
+### Live Verification
+- Mini `ruby scripts/SaneMaster.rb external_tools --json --timeout 30`:
+  - installed: `cass`, `ubs`
+  - missing: `dcg`, `br`/`bv`, `asb`
+  - `cass`: `installed_but_index_unhealthy`
+  - `ubs`: `installed_but_module_checksum_mismatch`
+- Mini direct `cass sessions --workspace ~/SaneApps/infra/SaneProcess --limit 3 --json` returned real SaneProcess session metadata.
+- Mini direct `cass search "SaneMaster external_tools" --workspace ~/SaneApps/infra/SaneProcess --limit 3 --json` returned no hits and warned that the Tantivy search index is missing.
+- Mini direct `cass index --full` found local Claude/Codex history but failed during lexical rebuild with a shard-count mismatch.
+- Mini direct `ubs --diff --format=json` failed before scanning because the fetched Ruby module checksum did not match the expected checksum.
+- Mini targeted `ruby scripts/sanemaster/external_tools_test.rb` -> `9/9`
+- Mini full `ruby scripts/SaneMaster.rb verify --timeout 900` -> passed:
+  - latest final line: `✅ Tests passed! (199 tests, 109s)`
+
+### Current State
+- SaneProcess now has a repeatable way to evaluate these external tools without adopting them as dependencies.
+- Current practical value:
+  - `cass` is useful for listing session metadata right now, but not for search until its index path is repaired.
+  - `ubs` is not usable yet because checksum verification blocks the Ruby scan module.
+- Nothing from this evaluation is wired into default `verify`, release, support, or status paths.
+
+### Next
+- Re-check `cass` after an upstream fix or a safe local index repair path exists.
+- Re-check `ubs` after the Ruby module checksum mismatch is resolved upstream or a pinned local module source is documented.
+- Keep `dcg`, `br`/`bv`, and `asb` optional/watch-only unless a concrete SaneProcess workflow needs them.
